{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>How.</b> [etc.] Behold, the prophet rebuked them and they did not listen." "<b>A harlot.</b> In place of a married woman, after she had been a faithful wife." "The yod [in] <b>I was filled with justice</b> is extra, like the yod [in] גנובתי יומה (Genesis 31:39)." "<b>Justice lodged in her, but now murderers.</b> The meaning is of standing time [i.e., the imperfect], for it has no sign in the sacred language." "<b>Murderers.</b> A verb going out to two objects, and the meaning refers to the judges."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:30.481784228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}